md(n,'> [!warning] Common CSP mistakes','The template must put the same generated value in each intended script element. The shown r4nd0mB64 string is only a placeholder; the Python generator supplies16randombytes. Registration must happen before serving requests.\n\n> [!warning] Common CSP mistakes','Nonceheaderalone blocksown scripts absenttemplatematching.')
md(n,"Adding `'unsafe-inline'` (without a nonce) or `'unsafe-eval'` to make errors go away undoes most of the protection.","Adding unsafe-inline without an effective nonce/hash weakens inline-script protection. Unsafe-eval separately enables string-to-code execution; neither means every other directive disappears.",'Avoidall-or-nothingeffectclaim.')
md(n,'Caching HTML that contains a nonce at a CDN effectively makes it static.','Reusing cached HTML/header nonce pairs makes that nonce reusable across those responses. Use a suitable hash policy for static content or generate matching fresh headers and HTML per response.','Cache scopequalifiesstaticforever claim.')
md(n,'the browser reports violations without blocking','the browser does not enforce that report-only policy; configured reporting may deliver violations','Reportdeliverynotautomaticwithoutendpoint; otherenforcedpoliciesstillblock.')
md(n,"makes dangerous sinks like `innerHTML` reject plain strings. Code must pass a `TrustedHTML` object created by a policy you define (which typically runs DOMPurify). That shrinks the code you must audit from \"every sink\" to \"a handful of policies\".","enforces Trusted Types at covered injection sinks in supporting browsers. Without an applicable default policy, ordinary strings passed to innerHTML are rejected. A default policy may instead convert strings. TrustedHTML is only as safe as the policy that creates it; restrict policy creation and audit policies, callers and downstream transformations.",'DefaultpolicyexceptionandTTnotautomaticsanitisation.')
md(n,'Reflected and stored XSS are inserted by the server; DOM XSS happens entirely in client JS, often from `location.hash`, invisible to the server.','Stored/reflected describe persistence; DOM-based describes a client-side source-to-sink flow. These categories can overlap, and DOM sources need not be invisible to the server.','Fixtakeawaytaxonomy.')
